        ":question/worked-solution": "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-2,8).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ and $y=8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 64 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-32x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-32x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-32 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{16}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
